-- title:
--   Integral point on the localised Hecke algebra after enlarging 𝒪
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$, let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers, and let $\mathcal{O}$ be a domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete with respect to the adic filtration of its maximal ideal, with finite residue field and of characteristic $0$. Assume (as a `Fact` hypothesis) that weight-two level-$\Gamma_0(N)$ cusp forms have an integral structure, i.e. that the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) spanned by those cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers is the whole space. Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$, to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a type $\mathcal{O}'$ carrying the same package of structures (commutative domain, discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal, finite residue field, characteristic $0$), together with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra structure making $\mathcal{O}'$ a finite $\mathcal{O}$-module with $\operatorname{algebraMap} \colon \mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}'$ a local homomorphism, such that this structure map is injective and such that there exists at least one $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra homomorphism $\mathrm{CuspForm.heckeLocal}\ N\ S\ \mathcal{O}'\ \theta' \to \mathcal{O}'$, where $\theta'$ is $\theta$ followed by the map of residue fields induced by $\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}'$, and where [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪' θ'`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) is by definition the localisation of `heckeBaseAlgebra N S 𝒪'` at the image under `latticeBaseChange N S 𝒪'` of the complement of the prime ideal `heckeCharKernel N S 𝒪' θ'`.
--
--   This is the statement that, after a finite extension of the coefficient ring, the Hecke algebra localised at a residual eigensystem $\theta$ admits an integral point, equivalently that some weight-two eigenform of level $N$ with coefficients in $\mathcal{O}'$ is congruent to $\theta$. It is used in the construction of the patching data for the modularity-lifting argument, being cited by the two `exists_patchingDatum_of_isResiduallyModular…` results.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_heckeLocal_exists_finite_extension_nonempty_algHom.lean

